# Redirects for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# A static export has no proxy, and `src/proxy.ts` is doing two jobs that have to
# survive the move: sending a visitor from an unprefixed URL to a language, and
# keeping the URLs this site published before the 2026 rebuild working. Every one
# of those is a line below. `npm run check:export` fails if any destination here
# was never built.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>. First match wins, so the specific rules come
# before the catch-alls.

# The bare domain. A 302 rather than a 301 because which language a first-time
# visitor should get is a decision that may change — and a 301 is cached by the
# browser forever, which would make changing it impossible for anyone who has
# been here once.
#
# This is the one thing the export cannot do as well as the proxy did: static
# rules cannot read Accept-Language, so everyone lands on English and switches
# from the header if they want Dutch. Doing it properly needs a Worker, which is
# worth it only if the analytics ever say it matters.
/                    /en             302

# URLs from before the rebuild, when English had no prefix. These have genuinely
# moved, so 301.
/about               /en/about       301
/work                /en/work        301
/work/*              /en/work/:splat 301

# The blog and the gallery are gone. Their links are not.
/blog                /en             301
/blog/*              /en             301
/gallery             /en             301
/en/blog             /en             301
/en/blog/*           /en             301
/nl/blog             /nl             301
/nl/blog/*           /nl             301
/en/gallery          /en             301
/nl/gallery          /nl             301
